> Although this is not intended to be supported, could not reproduce.

Oh, try adding `vim.o.signcolumn = "yes"`. Not sure what's going on, but if neovim is crashing, that's not really a mini issue:

```
NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1473+g9a29622b54
```

```lua
vim.pack.add({
  { src = "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim" },
})

vim.o.signcolumn = "yes"

local MiniStatuscolumn = require("mini.statuscolumn")
MiniStatuscolumn.setup({
  content = MiniStatuscolumn.gen_content.main({
    { format = "ssssssssss", sep = "" },
    --          1234567890
  }),
})
```

Like if `mini.statuscolumn` somehow exceeds 9 columns. Btw, it prints different errors - more like an error casino 🎰

> I feel like the `MiniStatuscolumn.gen_content.main()` spec is a little bit clunky and mixes different concepts together, but I do like how concise it is.

After trying to figure out what the hell I actually wanted to say, I realized it's not bad at all. I just need to think of them more as rules or overrides on top of the defaults. For some reason, I initially thought of `{ format = "=lfs", sep = "▏" }` as the main configuration separated from the other rules. But in practice, it's really just another rule that can be overridden multiple times, and since there are only two things used for filtering (`win` and `ltype`), the wrapper fields can basically be treated as visual noise.

<details><summary>Possible interfaces</summary>

```lua
-- 1. I don't like this
local spec = {
  default = {
    format = "=lfs",
    sep = "▏"
  },
  rules = {
    { when = { ltype = "virt" }, lnum = "•" },
    { when = { ltype = "wrap" }, lnum = "↳" },
    { when = { win = "inactive" }, sep = " " },
  },
}

-- 2. I'd prefer this
local spec = {
  format = "=lfs",
  sep = "▏",
  rules = {
    { when = { ltype = "virt" }, lnum = "•" },
    { when = { ltype = "wrap" }, lnum = "↳" },
    { when = { win = "inactive" }, sep = " " },
  },
}

-- 3. The same idea, but flat
local spec = {
  { format = "=lfs", sep = "▏" },
  { when = { ltype = "virt" }, lnum = "•" },
  { when = { ltype = "wrap" }, lnum = "↳" },
  { when = { win = "inactive" }, sep = " " },
}

-- 4. (current) Fine and concise, though it's a little disorganized
local spec = {
  { format = "=lfs", sep = "▏" },
  { ltype = "virt", lnum = "•" },
  { ltype = "wrap", lnum = "↳" },
  { win = "inactive", sep = " " },
}

-- 5. Explicit, either forces an order or introduces weird internal priorities
local spec = {
  { win = "both", ltype = "all", format = "=lfs", sep = "▏" },
  { win = "both", ltype = "virt", lnum = "•" },
  { win = "both", ltype = "wrap", lnum = "↳" },
  { win = "inactive", ltype = "all", sep = " " },
}
```

</details>
